WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:09.740
Control which machines can start remote agent workers, which projects they can reach, and how to revoke access immediately in Settings and Machines.

00:10.300 --> 00:26.140
Every machine card in Settings and Machines shows two named permission lines: one for agents on this machine starting work there, and one for agents on that machine starting work here. Joining stays one-way until you click Allow in reverse.

00:26.800 --> 00:41.200
Open Who can run work here on the receiving computer to label your own machine, restrict projects to linked or listed checkouts, choose allowed provider sign-ins, and cap access at read-only, supervised, or full access.

00:41.800 --> 00:55.160
Keep the three boundaries distinct: SpecWithCode Connect opens your threads across devices, machine worker grants let agents launch work remotely, and MCP attaches external tools per project.

00:55.800 --> 01:03.320
Lowering a permission level or clicking Revoke takes effect right away so remote agents cannot start new runs.
